# 43. Role Dashboards: Radiology (RIS), Blood Bank & Dialysis

Roles: `radiology_manager`, `radiology_admin`, `radiology_receptionist`, `radiology_scheduler`, `radiology_prep_staff`, `radiology_technician`, `xray_technician`, `ct_technician`, `mri_technician`, `us_technician`, `mammo_technician`, `radiologist`, `reporting_assistant`, `pacs_admin`, `radiology_billing_executive`, `equipment_manager`, + `blood_bank_admin`, `dialysis_admin`.
**Family rule (RIS):** DICOM worklist-first, dose logging, critical-finding closure, PACS viewer sessions audited. Current RIS specs: **0 tasks** per role: add task lists. `radiology_admin` = manager view.

### Radiology Manager / Admin (`radiology_manager`)
- **Purpose:** Department throughput, TAT, utilisation, dose, revenue.
- **Current status:** spec `risDashboardSpec` · route `/radiology/dashboard/radiology_manager` · current depth: 8 KPIs / 0 tasks / 3 alerts / 6 queues / 7 actions / 5 modules
- **KPI cards (target):** Studies today by modality; Report TAT (median/90th pct); Scanner utilisation %; Critical findings unacked; Repeat/reject %; Revenue per modality; Pending reports backlog; Equipment uptime
- **Worklists / queues:** Modality worklists; Report backlog by radiologist; Critical findings log; Preparation queue; Equipment downtime
- **Alerts:** Critical finding unacked; TAT breach; Scanner down; Dose outlier
- **Quick actions:** Reassign reports, Open PACS, Schedule slot, Log downtime
- **Sections / tabs:** Overview · Modalities · TAT · Dose · Equipment · Revenue
- **Features:** Modality dashboard (CT/MRI/XR/US/Mammo); Radiation dose log & outlier alert; Structured-report templates; Report-centre MIS; PACS/DICOM health
- **Data / APIs:** `/radiology/*`, `/radiology/dicom/*`, RIS spec modules
- **Permissions & privacy:** Studies with patient IDs; clinical role.

